id: pm-ts-starter-min-sdk-drift
title: Compile packed contracts against each exact selected SDK bound
description: "Follow-up to PR 153: packed declarations resolved SDK imports from a current-only consumer installation, leaving the minimum bound untested. Isolate each runtime and bound, verify the installed resolution, and regress a current-only public SDK API."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-ts-starter#154"
created_at: "2026-10-24T13:07:42.652Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T16:49:40.242Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Exact manifest minimum and explicit current SDK resolve inside separate packed npm and Bun consumers; a newer-only public API passes current and fails minimum; reverting only consumer provisioning fails the regression.
comments[24]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-24T13:07:46.558Z",codex-agent,"Scope: correct the packed-consumer compatibility gate added by PR 153. Use separate npm and Bun consumer installations per bound, select the minimum from manifest.json and current release 2026.10.24, and prove the actual resolver result from each consumer. Add a real newer-only SDK API use through emitted declarations, retaining the fixed compiler examples and no-git checks. Repository dependency pins remain unchanged; full npm and Bun release gates will run locally and in CI."
  "2026-10-24T13:07:47.361Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: each compiler project maps the selected SDK public type exports through TypeScript paths, including imports reached through absolute external declarations. Unexported SDK subpaths resolve to an empty declaration rather than falling through to a foreign installation. Packed acceptance now installs npm and Bun consumers separately for each exact bound and verifies package metadata and SDK entry resolution at runtime. Regression uses real acquireLockLease, absent in the manifest minimum and present in 2026.10.24. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstring gate and zero-duplication gate passed."
  "2026-10-24T13:07:47.949Z",codex-agent,"Fail-on-revert proof: restored only checkSdkContracts to its origin/main implementation, leaving the new regression and helper intact. node --test --test-name-pattern='absolute declaration imports report newer-only SDK APIs as minimum drift' test/sdk-contracts.test.ts failed 1/1: expected matrix.ok=false, got true, because the minimum inherited acquireLockLease from the external consumer's current SDK. Restored the fixed function immediately. Before revert the complete targeted suite passed 8/8 with 100% sdk-contracts.ts lines, branches and functions. Running the registered targeted suite again after restoration. Local strict tracker health passes after provisioning the same pm-github version as CI; an existing provenance advisory remains untouched."
  "2026-10-24T13:07:48.526Z",codex-agent,"Restored implementation verified through the registered command: npx pm test pm-ts-starter-min-sdk-drift --run --progress --env-clear npm_config_allow_scripts --env-clear NPM_CONFIG_ALLOW_SCRIPTS passed 8/8 with zero failures/skips and 100% module lines/branches/functions. pm test without these overrides injects an npm allow-scripts setting rejected by project-scoped installs (EALLOWSCRIPTS); this runner UX gap is outside the product fix. Existing result tracking is disabled, so this comment retains the receipt. Full npm release gate is running with an isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git config; Bun will follow."
  "2026-10-24T13:07:49.170Z",codex-agent,"Local full npm gate passed: env HOME=<tmp> GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check. Repository suite: 367/367 tests, zero failures/skips, 100% lines/branches/functions over 9 required source files, 0% duplication, zero production audit vulnerabilities; packing, changelog and release-verification checks passed. Equivalent isolated Bun release gate is running. Product changes are ready for review; CI must confirm both runtimes on the final head."
  "2026-10-24T13:07:49.785Z",codex-agent,"Local full Bun release gate also passed with isolated HOME and global/system Git config disabled: 367/367 tests, zero failures/skips, unchanged 100% lines/branches/functions over 9 source files, 0% duplication, zero production vulnerabilities, packing, changelog and release-verification checks passed. Both local release gates are complete. Publication is pending owner approval to redact an accidentally expanded temporary path from this new, uncommitted item history; no existing published history was changed, and nothing has been committed or pushed. The implementation, regression, revert proof and PR text are prepared. Claim released while the narrow privacy exception is pending."
  "2026-10-24T13:07:50.477Z",codex-agent,"Owner-authorized privacy correction: deleted only this new, uncommitted item and its new history file, then recreated both through the pinned pm CLI with identical title, description, acceptance criteria, file/doc/test links and sanitized comments. No history lines were hand-edited and no previously committed history was changed. Temporary directory details use <tmp>. The completed local targeted and full npm/Bun gates remain valid; publication work has resumed."
  "2026-10-24T13:07:51.277Z",codex-agent,"Re-recorded fail-on-revert evidence from the completed experiment: node --test --test-name-pattern='absolute declaration imports report newer-only SDK APIs as minimum drift' test/sdk-contracts.test.ts failed 1/1 when only checkSdkContracts was restored to origin/main. The assertion expected matrix.ok=false but received true. The fixed function was restored, and the registered targeted suite then passed 8/8 with 100% module lines, branches and functions. The actual newer-only public API is acquireLockLease: current 2026.10.24 compiles; manifest minimum 2026.10.17 reports TS2551."
  "2026-10-24T13:09:05.256Z",codex-agent,"Privacy verification after authorized recreation: pm history pm-ts-starter-min-sdk-drift --verify --strict-exit passed with a matching current-item hash. The repository privacy/identity scan, node --test test/identity-audit.test.ts under isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git config, passed 4/4. Strict tracker health passed; the pre-existing provenance advisory remains unchanged. Changelog regeneration and check passed. Full staged-diff scanning for absolute filesystem paths, private identities and hostnames will run before each commit."
  "2026-10-24T13:10:39.618Z",codex-agent,"Ready-for-review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ts-starter/pull/154 . Product commit 8c1e899 contains the exact-bound SDK resolution fix, runtime version assertions, newer-only API regression, docs, emitted output and recreated tracker evidence. Post-commit repository identity/privacy scan passed 4/4. The complete staged diff had zero absolute filesystem paths, private network addresses, local username or hostname matches. Both local release gates already passed 367/367 with unchanged thresholds. CI must finish the full npm and Bun gates on Node 22 and 26 at the final head; no merge or release is authorized. Claim released for orchestrator review; item remains in progress."
  "2026-10-24T14:29:04.798Z",codex-agent,"Review round: reproduce the empty-module fallback accepting unresolved SDK namespace imports, remove fabricated declarations, bind all SDK resolution to each selected published exports map, and add a two-bound mutation table plus an intentionally blinded-resolution self-test. Verify targeted tests, typecheck, lint, behavioral revert, and exact pushed CI npm/Bun release gates. Remote branch is current and already contains origin/main; no merge is needed."
  "2026-10-24T14:36:15.440Z",codex-agent,"Implementation now removes the empty declaration and delegates exports resolution to real TypeScript namespace probes scoped to the selected SDK, with no paths mapping in the probes. Only natively resolved files are rebound into external declarations. Probe failures retain real TypeScript codes even when dependency skipLibCheck would hide an unresolved import. Mutation controls cover eight cases at both 2026.10.17 and 2026.10.24: nonexistent subpath, removed exported subpath, misspelled package (TS2307); missing named/type-only exports (TS2305); type exported without a runtime value (TS2693); type-only import used as a value (TS1361); default versus namespace import (TS1192). Good authoring/read/namespace consumers must pass. Additional tests cover minimum-only subpath removal, hidden unresolved external imports, native string/conditional/wildcard/null/missing-file exports, and self-test rejection of both a blind compiler and a stubbed resolution probe. Typecheck, test compilation, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication checks passed before final behavioral verification."
  "2026-10-24T14:39:06.773Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replaced only sdk-contracts.ts with its pre-review HEAD implementation; kept all new tests and docs unchanged. Ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"resolution self-test|external declaration subpaths|native SDK exports\" test/sdk-contracts.test.ts. Exit 1, all 3 regressions failed: mutation table detected only 12/16 drifts (nonexistent and removed namespace subpaths were accepted); external minimum-only removal reported 0 drift rows instead of 1; native null export crashed in the old exports parser. Immediately restored the fixed source in a finally block and verified its bytes matched the saved fix. Tests import the TypeScript source, so no reverted build artifact was needed. Earlier fixed checker suite passed 10/10 with 100% module lines/branches/functions; the final added exports and resolution-stub controls passed 2/2. Running the complete registered suite after restoration."
  "2026-10-24T14:45:08.657Z",codex-agent,"Post-restore registered verification passed: pm test pm-ts-starter-min-sdk-drift --run --progress --env-clear npm_config_allow_scripts --env-clear NPM_CONFIG_ALLOW_SCRIPTS --timeout 1200 executed node --test --experimental-test-coverage --test-coverage-include=sdk-contracts.ts test/sdk-contracts.test.ts: 11/11 passed, zero failures/skips/cancellations, 100% checker lines/branches/functions. This includes all 16 mutation drifts, all 6 good consumer controls, minimum-only removal, unresolved external declarations, native export-map forms, blind-compiler rejection, resolver-only-stub rejection, exact packed npm/Bun acceptance, and no-git concurrency checks. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run lint, npm run duplication and npm run docstring passed. History verification and strict tracker health passed; existing provenance advisory is unchanged. Remote main remains included. Starting full release gates with isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git config after changelog regeneration."
  "2026-10-24T14:55:17.934Z",codex-agent,"Both full local release gates passed: npm run release:check and bun run release:check, each with an isolated HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null, GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1, and npm_config_allow_scripts/NPM_CONFIG_ALLOW_SCRIPTS cleared. Each gate passed 370/370 tests with zero failures/skips/cancellations, unchanged 100% lines/branches/functions across all 9 required source files, 0% duplication, documented declarations, zero production audit vulnerabilities, packed dry run, changelog check and both release-verification checks. Targeted registered suite passed 11/11 with 100% checker lines/branches/functions. Fix-only revert proof is recorded above (3/3 regressions failed, then fix restored). Preparing a privacy-scanned implementation/evidence commit; final pushed-head CI npm/Bun receipts will be linked in PR 154. Existing tracker provenance advisory is unchanged; no new CLI/SDK defect was encountered. Item stays in progress for orchestrator verification; no merge or release."
  "2026-10-24T15:04:12.148Z",codex-agent,"Additional class-level probe found a real remaining blind spot: an unresolved SDK subpath containing an apostrophe inside an external declaration returned ok=true at both bounds because the trace parser stopped at the apostrophe. CI on the first implementation head is still running, but it is not final evidence. Reclaiming to parse complete resolution records, including quoted and multiline specifiers, and add regressions before final verification."
  "2026-10-24T15:08:03.765Z",codex-agent,"Parser correction: collect complete TypeScript resolution records rather than stopping at apostrophes; preserve complete selected specifier names when reading native resolved paths. External declaration cases now include quoted, multiline and delimiter-like missing SDK subpaths (TS2307 at both published bounds), plus a valid quoted exported alias that must pass. Targeted tests passed 2/2 through pm test --run --only-last --progress after restoration. Parser-only revert proof: restored only sdk-contracts.ts to commit 53c436e while keeping the extended tests; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"external declaration subpaths\" test/sdk-contracts.test.ts failed 1/1, reporting 0 drift rows instead of 2 for the quoted missing subpath. Restored the corrected parser in a finally block and verified identical source bytes. npm run typecheck, npm run lint and npm run duplication passed (0% duplication). Repeating both complete isolated release gates before the final correction commit."
  "2026-10-24T15:17:41.572Z",codex-agent,"Final corrected-parser release gates both passed: npm run release:check and bun run release:check under isolated HOME, disabled global/system Git config, and cleared npm script-allow overrides. Each passed 370/370 tests (including all 11 SDK contract tests), zero failures/skips/cancellations, unchanged 100% lines/branches/functions across all 9 required source files, 0% duplication and zero production vulnerabilities. Packing, changelog and release checks passed. The registered extended parser checks passed 2/2 after the parser-only revert proof, while the original fix-only proof failed all 3 regressions. All 16 primary mutation rows drift and all 6 unmodified controls pass; additional external quoted/multiline/delimiter-like imports drift at both bounds and a valid quoted export passes. Preparing the final privacy-scanned correction commit, then final-head CI npm/Bun verification and PR receipts. Claim released for orchestrator review; existing provenance advisory is unchanged."
  "2026-10-24T16:05:24.698Z",codex-agent,"Review round 2: remove all compiler trace parsing. Preserve exact selected-SDK binding for external declaration graphs, fail closed on malformed or unresolved specifiers, add hostile consumer and declaration fuzz controls, and prove the regression by reverting only the fix. Remote head is current with main; dependency pins remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-24T16:18:47.677Z",codex-agent,"Replaced all resolution trace parsing with structured compiler AST imports and JSON exports resolution under the types condition beside each selected SDK. Unresolved selected exports immediately drift with TS2307; successfully resolved files alone are rebound. A final full declaration-graph probe uses skipLibCheck=false and reads only diagnostic-line error codes, including missing modules/exports/types and syntax failures. Structured graph tooling is bounded and fails with compiler_unavailable when absent or malformed. Existing native-export-map, real export-removal and newer-only API controls pass. Added a 16-name hostile table across both consumers and external declarations at both bounds, plus external named-export and resolution-stub controls. Test fixture declarations are imported through their emitted JavaScript specifiers so TypeScript declaration-import diagnostics cannot mask a broken resolver."
  "2026-10-24T16:26:27.370Z",codex-agent,"Fix-only behavioral revert proof: replaced only sdk-contracts.ts with the reviewed HEAD implementation, leaving the new tests unchanged. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"hostile specifier fuzz|external named-export\" test/sdk-contracts.test.ts exited 1: both regressions failed (0 passed, 2 failed). The old checker detected only 28/32 hostile external declaration rows, accepting four unresolved rows; the external named-export mutation incorrectly returned ok=true. Restored the fixed source in a finally block and verified its SHA256 matched the saved bytes. The fixed fuzz and resolution-stub controls previously passed 2/2; final registered verification follows. An intermediate complete targeted run exposed a packed Bun runtime timeout and a new branch-coverage gap; these are being resolved before publication."
  "2026-10-24T16:32:19.860Z",codex-agent,"Bun compatibility is fixed by using the asynchronous structured compiler API inside bounded private workers. Final focused verification passed 5/5: all 64 hostile consumer/declaration rows, external missing exports with a resolution-stub self-test, TS2724 and missing declaration TS7016 controls, malformed graph tooling refusals, and packed npm/Bun acceptance at both exact SDK bounds with no tools on PATH. No timeouts or coverage thresholds were relaxed. Typecheck, test compilation, lint, docstrings and 0% duplication pass. Running the complete registered checker suite with an LCOV receipt before pushing; full npm and Bun release-gate evidence will come from exact-head CI."
  "2026-10-24T16:43:28.869Z",codex-agent,"Complete registered checker run measured 100% lines/branches/functions and passed all 14 non-packed tests; the packed matrix exceeded its old 30-second parent-process deadline under the runner. The focused packed matrix had already passed outside that wrapper. Increased only the packed integration parent deadline to 120 seconds because it performs multiple independently bounded compiler/graph checks. Each product tooling invocation remains limited to 30 seconds and 8 MiB; coverage thresholds remain 100%. Added runtime/bound context to timeout assertions. Re-running the packed acceptance through the pm runner before publication. The existing linked test command is immutable, so its standard coverage summary is retained rather than changing its reporter; full CI produces the repository LCOV evidence."
  "2026-10-24T16:49:39.297Z",codex-agent,"Final local verification: the corrected packed acceptance passed 1/1 through pm test --run --only-last --progress with npm script-allow variables cleared. All four npm/Bun and minimum/current consumer combinations passed their exact installed SDK metadata/entry assertions, matrices, CLI activation and no-tools-on-PATH runs. The complete prior registered run passed all 14 other tests and measured 100% checker lines/branches/functions; its only failure was the now-corrected packed parent deadline. Typecheck, test compilation, lint, docstrings, 0% duplication and isolated identity/privacy tests (4/4) pass. Fix-only revert proof remains recorded (2/2 regressions fail with the old checker; fixed source restored); tests import TypeScript source directly. Full npm/Bun gates will be verified in exact-head CI. No new pm CLI/SDK defect was found; the existing tracker provenance advisory remains unchanged. Preparing the privacy-scanned implementation and PM evidence commit, then releasing this claim for orchestrator verification without closing the item."
